-- =====================================================================
--  Unika Kebab — neighbourhood landing page content
--
--  Five local pages. Only the first is active: the rest are drafts and are
--  published one batch at a time from Admin -> Neighbourhoods, which is a
--  deliberate choice rather than an oversight (see docs/SEO-CHECKLIST.md).
--
--  Re-runnable: each row is upserted on its slug, so editing a page in the
--  admin panel and then re-running this file would overwrite it. Run it once,
--  then edit in the admin panel.
-- =====================================================================

-- King West
INSERT INTO `neighbourhoods` (`slug`, `name`, `batch`, `sort_order`, `is_active`, `page_title`, `meta_desc`, `meta_keywords`, `og_image`, `og_image_alt`, `hero_eyebrow`, `hero_title`, `hero_text`, `hero_image`, `hero_image_alt`, `intro_title`, `intro_text`, `travel_title`, `travel_text`, `fact1_icon`, `fact1_label`, `fact1_text`, `fact2_icon`, `fact2_label`, `fact2_text`, `fact3_icon`, `fact3_label`, `fact3_text`, `fact4_icon`, `fact4_label`, `fact4_text`, `picks_title`, `picks_text`, `pick1_dish`, `pick1_note`, `pick2_dish`, `pick2_note`, `pick3_dish`, `pick3_note`, `faq1_q`, `faq1_a`, `faq2_q`, `faq2_a`, `faq3_q`, `faq3_a`, `closing_title`, `closing_text`, `neighbours`) VALUES
  ('kebab-in-king-west-toronto', 'King West', 1, 1, 1, 'Kebab Near King West — Westbound 504 to Jefferson Ave', 'Halal Turkish charcoal kebab 1.6 km west of King and Bathurst. Westbound 504 King, no transfer, off at King St W at Jefferson Ave. Open 12 to 9 daily, pickup.', 'kebab king west, halal kebab king west toronto, turkish restaurant king west, charcoal kebab toronto', 'assets/img/hero-home.jpg', 'Kebab skewers over charcoal at Unika Kebab, Liberty Village', 'Westbound 504 King · Bathurst to Jefferson Ave', 'Stay on the 504 west past Bathurst. Dinner is ten minutes on.', 'Unika Kebab is a family-run halal Turkish charcoal grill at 133 Jefferson Ave, about 1.6 km west of King and Bathurst. One streetcar, no transfer, off at King St W at Jefferson Ave. Open 12 to 9, seven days. Pickup only.', 'assets/img/hero-home.jpg', 'Charcoal-grilled kebab skewers at Unika Kebab, a 504 King ride from King West', 'The King Street corridor ends at Bathurst. We are west of that.', 'The King Street Transit Priority Corridor runs 2.6 km, Jarvis to Bathurst, and then it stops. West of Bathurst your streetcar goes back to sharing the road with everyone else. That last stretch is the one that brings you to us: about 1.6 km further west, at 133 Jefferson Ave, on the block beside Allan A. Lamport Stadium. Ten minutes or so on a westbound 504, no transfer, no walk at the far end.

Unika Kebab is a family-run Turkish charcoal grill, fully halal. The address is Liberty Village rather than King West — one grill, one counter, nothing on your side of Bathurst. Every order is shaped and put over live coals after you ask for it, which is why a plate takes longer than you expect and tastes like it did. Beef kofte, Adana, chicken shawarma, shish tavuk, falafel. That is the list, and it stays that short on purpose.

You already live beside this kind of thing. Draper Street still has its Second Empire cottages from 1881 and 1882, twenty-eight of them, a designated heritage district a few steps off Wellington. Victoria Memorial Square at Portland and Wellington West is the oldest surviving European burying ground in Toronto, used from 1794 to 1863, now a few worn markers around a cenotaph. Small stubborn survivors under a brand new skyline. We are one of those with a charcoal grill attached. Plan around one thing: the grill goes cold at nine, seven nights a week.', 'One streetcar west, no transfer — and one date to watch', 'Board a westbound 504 King anywhere along your stretch — Spadina, Portland, Bathurst — and stay on it. Past Strachan, past Shaw. When Lamport Stadium opens up along the south side of King, the next stop is yours: King St W at Jefferson Ave. Reach Dufferin and you have gone past. From Bathurst reckon on about ten minutes; from Spadina, twelve to fifteen in the evening peak, because priority ends at Bathurst and the last leg runs in ordinary traffic. On foot it is about 1.6 km due west along King, roughly twenty-two minutes.

One date worth knowing: from 1 November 2026 the TTC has the 504 diverting via Queen Street West between Spadina and Roncesvalles while the watermain and track under King are rebuilt, with 504C replacement buses on King. Portland to Spadina is one of the dig zones. Check ttc.ca before you set out.', 'fa-solid fa-train', 'One car, no transfer', 'Westbound 504 King from Spadina, Portland or Bathurst to the stop named King St W at Jefferson Ave. Roughly ten minutes from Bathurst, no transfer, and the door is right there.', 'fa-solid fa-traffic-light', 'Priority ends at Bathurst', 'The King Street Transit Priority Corridor is 2.6 km, Jarvis to Bathurst. West of Bathurst the streetcar shares the road with cars again, so add a few minutes to a 5:30 departure.', 'fa-solid fa-person-walking', '1.6 km, straight west', 'King and Bathurst to our door is about 1.6 km, due west along King St W past Strachan and Shaw. Call it twenty-two minutes at an unhurried pace.', 'fa-solid fa-clock', 'Pickup only, closed at nine', 'Order through Square or Google for pickup, or call 416-516-2087. No delivery apps. Leave Portland Street on a westbound car by about 8:20 and you will still be served; we stop at 21:00.', 'Eat it here, or eat it on the 504?', 'One question decides your order: table or streetcar. Plates want a chair, and the ride back east is eight or nine minutes of standing. So this trio splits three ways — one to carry, one to sit down with, and one that genuinely does not care how long the journey takes.', 'Sandwiches::Shish Tavuk Shawarma', '$11.99. Marinated chicken straight off the coals, wrapped tight. The one thing here we would hand you to eat standing on a rush-hour 504 heading back to Bathurst.', 'Plates (Platter)::Chicken Shawarma', 'The $19.99 plate. You have come 1.6 km west for dinner — take the chair and the rice, not a container balanced on your knees between Strachan and Spadina.', 'Dessert::Baklava', 'The only order that improves by sitting still. Add it to the bag, ride home, eat it on a Portland Street stoop an hour later. Pastry does not mind the streetcar.', 'Which stop do I actually get off at?', 'King St W at Jefferson Ave. Coming from the east you pass Strachan and Shaw, then Allan A. Lamport Stadium fills the south side of King — 1155 King St W, sitting between Fraser Ave and Jefferson Ave. Jefferson is the street at the far end of it, and the stop is right there. We are a few doors down at 133 Jefferson Ave. If the car gets to Dufferin, you have gone past us.', 'Does the 504 actually move at 5:30, or should I just walk?', 'Depends how packed it is. Transit priority on King ends at Bathurst, so the whole western leg runs in ordinary traffic and can stretch well past ten minutes in the evening peak. The walk is about 1.6 km straight west along King, roughly twenty-two minutes. If two full cars go by without room, walking wins. Either way a 5:30 start gets you here with hours to spare.', 'Can I come after drinks on Portland Street?', 'Only if it is the first round. The grill is off at 21:00, seven nights a week, and the kitchen needs you through the door before that. Treat this as a 6:30 or 7:00 trip and you get a table, a proper plate and a slow ride home. Treat it as a nightcap and you will find the shutter down.', 'Order first, then get on the streetcar', '133 Jefferson Ave, Toronto. Open 12:00 to 21:00, seven days. Order for pickup through Square or Google, or phone 416-516-2087, then ride a westbound 504 King and get off at King St W at Jefferson Ave — the stop just past Lamport Stadium as you come from the east. Order before you board and the bag is waiting when you walk in. One streetcar from Bathurst, no transfer, about ten minutes.', 'kebab-in-fort-york-toronto,kebab-in-queen-west-toronto')
