-- Parkdale
INSERT INTO `neighbourhoods` (`slug`, `name`, `batch`, `sort_order`, `is_active`, `page_title`, `meta_desc`, `meta_keywords`, `og_image`, `og_image_alt`, `hero_eyebrow`, `hero_title`, `hero_text`, `hero_image`, `hero_image_alt`, `intro_title`, `intro_text`, `travel_title`, `travel_text`, `fact1_icon`, `fact1_label`, `fact1_text`, `fact2_icon`, `fact2_label`, `fact2_text`, `fact3_icon`, `fact3_label`, `fact3_text`, `fact4_icon`, `fact4_label`, `fact4_text`, `picks_title`, `picks_text`, `pick1_dish`, `pick1_note`, `pick2_dish`, `pick2_note`, `pick3_dish`, `pick3_note`, `faq1_q`, `faq1_a`, `faq2_q`, `faq2_a`, `faq3_q`, `faq3_a`, `closing_title`, `closing_text`, `neighbours`) VALUES
  ('kebab-in-parkdale-toronto', 'Parkdale', 2, 2, 0, 'Halal Charcoal Kebab a Short Walk East of Parkdale', 'Turkish halal charcoal kebab about a kilometre east of Parkdale: 133 Jefferson Ave, just west of Lamport Stadium. Walk from Queen and Dufferin. Noon to 9 daily.', 'kebab parkdale, halal kebab parkdale toronto, turkish food parkdale, shawarma parkdale', 'uploads/site/about_20260728_125447_4dd2b2.png', 'Kofte shaped by hand in the Unika Kebab kitchen', 'For anyone walking east from Queen and Dufferin', 'The kebab at the other end of the Dufferin underpass', 'Unika Kebab is at 133 Jefferson Ave in Liberty Village — about a kilometre from Queen and Dufferin, or thirteen minutes on foot. Turkish charcoal, fully halal, family run. Open noon to 9pm, seven days, pickup only.', 'assets/img/bg-stone.jpg', 'Charcoal grill at Unika Kebab, a short walk east of Parkdale', 'One underpass, one turn east', 'Walk south on Dufferin from Queen and the sidewalk drops under the rail corridor — the 70-metre underpass that opened in November 2010 and finally retired the Dufferin Jog. Come up the other side, turn east on King, and you are six minutes from a charcoal grill. Past Mowat Ave, Jefferson Ave is the next street on your right. Allan A. Lamport Stadium starts just after it, so if you are level with the grandstand you have gone one street too far.

Parkdale reads a menu properly. The six blocks of Queen West from Sorauren Avenue to Roncesvalles are the centre of Little Tibet, home to the largest Tibetan community in North America, and the stretch east of there to Dufferin puts Sri Lankan, Ethiopian, Vietnamese and Polish counters within a few hundred metres of each other. People here ask what is in the sauce before they order. Halal is not a special request; it is a normal Tuesday. Unika Kebab sits east of all that, past the Parkdale Village BIA\'s edge at Dufferin, which means we are in Liberty Village and not in your neighbourhood — worth saying plainly before you put your shoes on.

What is here is Turkish charcoal, family run, fully halal. The kofte and the Adana get shaped and laid over the fire after your order goes in, which is why a full Saturday runs a few minutes long. Judge us on that.', 'South under the tracks, then east on King', 'On foot from the Queen St West at Dufferin St stop: south on Dufferin, through the underpass, then left onto King Street West. Past Mowat, Jefferson is the next street on your right, just before the stadium. About a kilometre, call it thirteen minutes at a normal pace.

Riding, the 29 Dufferin drops you at Dufferin St at King St West, which leaves roughly six minutes east on foot. From Jameson, Cowan or Roncesvalles the whole walk runs closer to twenty minutes, so most people take the 501 Queen east to Dufferin first and start from there. Lakeshore West GO riders can get off at Exhibition instead and come north in about six minutes.', 'fa-solid fa-train', '501 Queen', 'Ride east to Queen St West at Dufferin St, the far end of the Parkdale Village BIA, which runs Roncesvalles to Dufferin. About a kilometre on foot from there, roughly thirteen minutes.', 'fa-solid fa-bus-simple', '29 Dufferin', 'Board at Dufferin St at Queen St West and get off at Dufferin St at King St West. Then about six minutes east on King: past Mowat, right onto Jefferson, just before the stadium.', 'fa-solid fa-person-walking', 'Walking distances', 'About 1 km from Queen and Dufferin. Closer to 1.7 km, or roughly twenty minutes, from Queen and Jameson by Parkdale Collegiate Institute at 209 Jameson Ave.', 'fa-solid fa-clock', 'Noon to 9, seven days', 'Same hours every day, and 9pm is the hard stop. Pickup only — no delivery apps, no drivers of our own. Order on Square, through Google, or call 416-516-2087.', 'The order for people who read the whole menu', 'Half of Parkdale already knows what it wants from a kebab shop, so skip the obvious for a minute. These three tell you more about a kitchen than the Adana does, and none of them is the thing everybody orders first.', 'Sandwiches::Shish Tavuk Shawarma', '$11.99, chicken, and the honest test of a charcoal cook — no chili to hide behind and nothing to rescue it if the fire is wrong. Order it before you order anything spicy.', 'Sides::Tabuli Bowl', 'Ordered on its own, not as a side. Tabuli is the one thing on the board the grill cannot rescue, which makes it the fastest way to learn how a kitchen preps in the morning.', 'Add-Ons::Extra Taratur Sauce', 'Taratur and garlic are not interchangeable. Get the extra taratur on the side, tear the sandwich in half, and settle which one you actually want. Cheapest decision on the board.', 'Is it quicker to walk from Queen and Dufferin, or take the 29?', 'Walk, most of the time. From the Queen St West at Dufferin St stop it is about a kilometre — thirteen minutes, south under the tracks and east on King. The 29 Dufferin only carries you as far as Dufferin St at King St West, and you still have six minutes east on foot after you step off. Coming from Jameson or Roncesvalles the maths flips: ride the 501 Queen to Dufferin, then walk the last stretch.', 'I\'m at the Sorauren market on a Monday. Can I still make it?', 'Yes, with room to spare. The Sorauren Farmers\' Market at 50 Wabash Ave runs Monday afternoons in season and wraps up at 7pm; we grill until 9pm and then we are finished for the night. Nine means nine — charcoal out, shutters down, nothing here at eleven. From Sorauren Ave, take the 501 Queen east to Dufferin and walk the last kilometre.', 'Is the whole kitchen halal, and is there anything for the vegetarians?', 'The whole kitchen is halal, not a section of it — one grill, one kitchen, family run. For a mixed table the Falafel sandwich is $10 and the Falafel Plate is $17.99, both vegetarian, with the Tabuli Bowl, Fries and Rice alongside them at $6. One order covers everybody, instead of splitting the group across two counters on Queen West.', '133 Jefferson Ave, before the stadium, until nine', '133 Jefferson Ave, on the south side of King, the street just west of Allan A. Lamport Stadium. Noon to 9pm, every day of the week. Order ahead on Square or through Google\'s page, or call 416-516-2087 and we will have it ready to collect. About thirteen minutes from Queen and Dufferin if you walk it — and the same thirteen minutes back with a Shish Tavuk in your hand.', 'kebab-in-queen-west-toronto,kebab-in-exhibition-place-toronto')
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `name` = VALUES(`name`), `batch` = VALUES(`batch`), `sort_order` = VALUES(`sort_order`), `is_active` = VALUES(`is_active`), `page_title` = VALUES(`page_title`), `meta_desc` = VALUES(`meta_desc`), `meta_keywords` = VALUES(`meta_keywords`), `og_image` = VALUES(`og_image`), `og_image_alt` = VALUES(`og_image_alt`), `hero_eyebrow` = VALUES(`hero_eyebrow`), `hero_title` = VALUES(`hero_title`), `hero_text` = VALUES(`hero_text`), `hero_image` = VALUES(`hero_image`), `hero_image_alt` = VALUES(`hero_image_alt`), `intro_title` = VALUES(`intro_title`), `intro_text` = VALUES(`intro_text`), `travel_title` = VALUES(`travel_title`), `travel_text` = VALUES(`travel_text`), `fact1_icon` = VALUES(`fact1_icon`), `fact1_label` = VALUES(`fact1_label`), `fact1_text` = VALUES(`fact1_text`), `fact2_icon` = VALUES(`fact2_icon`), `fact2_label` = VALUES(`fact2_label`), `fact2_text` = VALUES(`fact2_text`), `fact3_icon` = VALUES(`fact3_icon`), `fact3_label` = VALUES(`fact3_label`), `fact3_text` = VALUES(`fact3_text`), `fact4_icon` = VALUES(`fact4_icon`), `fact4_label` = VALUES(`fact4_label`), `fact4_text` = VALUES(`fact4_text`), `picks_title` = VALUES(`picks_title`), `picks_text` = VALUES(`picks_text`), `pick1_dish` = VALUES(`pick1_dish`), `pick1_note` = VALUES(`pick1_note`), `pick2_dish` = VALUES(`pick2_dish`), `pick2_note` = VALUES(`pick2_note`), `pick3_dish` = VALUES(`pick3_dish`), `pick3_note` = VALUES(`pick3_note`), `faq1_q` = VALUES(`faq1_q`), `faq1_a` = VALUES(`faq1_a`), `faq2_q` = VALUES(`faq2_q`), `faq2_a` = VALUES(`faq2_a`), `faq3_q` = VALUES(`faq3_q`), `faq3_a` = VALUES(`faq3_a`), `closing_title` = VALUES(`closing_title`), `closing_text` = VALUES(`closing_text`), `neighbours` = VALUES(`neighbours`);

-- Exhibition Place
INSERT INTO `neighbourhoods` (`slug`, `name`, `batch`, `sort_order`, `is_active`, `page_title`, `meta_desc`, `meta_keywords`, `og_image`, `og_image_alt`, `hero_eyebrow`, `hero_title`, `hero_text`, `hero_image`, `hero_image_alt`, `intro_title`, `intro_text`, `travel_title`, `travel_text`, `fact1_icon`, `fact1_label`, `fact1_text`, `fact2_icon`, `fact2_label`, `fact2_text`, `fact3_icon`, `fact3_label`, `fact3_text`, `fact4_icon`, `fact4_label`, `fact4_text`, `picks_title`, `picks_text`, `pick1_dish`, `pick1_note`, `pick2_dish`, `pick2_note`, `pick3_dish`, `pick3_note`, `faq1_q`, `faq1_a`, `faq2_q`, `faq2_a`, `faq3_q`, `faq3_a`, `closing_title`, `closing_text`, `neighbours`) VALUES
  ('kebab-in-exhibition-place-toronto', 'Exhibition Place', 2, 3, 0, 'Halal Kebab Near Exhibition Place, 6 Min From Exhibition GO', 'Halal charcoal kebab six minutes north of Exhibition GO, across the rail corridor at 133 Jefferson Ave. Order pickup before the Ex, BMO Field or the Coliseum.', 'kebab exhibition place, food near bmo field, halal food near ontario place, kebab before the game toronto', 'assets/img/hero-contact.jpg', 'Unika Kebab charcoal grill near BMO Field and Exhibition Place', 'Across the rail corridor from Exhibition Place', 'Kebab first on Jefferson Ave, then down to the Ex', '133 Jefferson Ave sits one block north of the rail corridor, about six minutes from the Atlantic Ave entrance to Exhibition GO. Charcoal grill, halal, open 12 to 9 every day — which makes us a before-your-event stop, not an after.', 'assets/img/hero-contact.jpg', 'Unika Kebab, a ten minute walk from the Exhibition Place gates', 'Start with the clock, not the menu', 'Work out your start time before you think about dinner. We close at 9pm, seven days, and Exhibition Place runs on evening schedules: a 7:30 kickoff at BMO Field, a show at the Coca-Cola Coliseum on Manitoba Drive, CNE grounds open until midnight through the run from late August to Labour Day. None of that finishes while our grill is on. So we are a before, not an after, and ninety minutes ahead of your gate is comfortable.

The shop is across the rail corridor from all of it. 133 Jefferson Ave, one block north of the tracks in Liberty Village, on the street that runs up the west side of Lamport Stadium. There is one Unika Kebab and this is it. About six minutes on foot from the Atlantic Ave entrance to Exhibition GO, about ten from Exhibition Loop, a little over twenty from the Princes\' Gates at Strachan and Lake Shore.

The rest is straightforward. Turkish, fully halal, family run. Skewers go on the charcoal when your order comes in, which is why there is a wait and why the place smells the way it does — kofte shaped by hand, chicken carved off the grill. On an event day that wait is the one thing worth planning around, so put the order in ahead and let the grill work happen before you arrive.', 'Three ways across the tracks', 'The corridor is the whole problem, and Exhibition GO is the way through it. Use the station\'s north entrance on Atlantic Ave, just south of Liberty Street — Metrolinx opened it in September 2024 and it is the shortest crossing. From there, east on Liberty St, then north up Jefferson. About six minutes. Lamport Stadium is your landmark; Jefferson runs up its west side.

From Exhibition Loop on Manitoba Drive, where the 509 Harbourfront and 511 Bathurst both end, it is roughly ten minutes on foot back through the station. From the Princes\' Gates, a little over twenty, or ride west to the loop first. And the part that belongs here rather than in the sales pitch: we are not on the grounds. This is a walk off-site and back, so if you are holding a ticket, ask at your gate about re-entry before you leave.', 'fa-solid fa-train', 'Exhibition GO, Atlantic Ave exit', 'Exhibition GO is on the Lakeshore West line. Its north entrance on Atlantic Ave, just south of Liberty St, opened in September 2024 — about six minutes on foot from our door.', 'fa-solid fa-train-subway', 'Both streetcars end at the loop', 'The 509 Harbourfront and 511 Bathurst both terminate at Exhibition Loop on Manitoba Drive, beside the Coca-Cola Coliseum at 45 Manitoba Dr. Roughly ten minutes on foot from there.', 'fa-solid fa-route', 'The stop is named after our street', 'The streetcar stop out front is named King St W at Jefferson Ave, on the 504 King. From Dufferin St at King it is six minutes east on foot. Check ttc.ca for diversions first.', 'fa-solid fa-clock', 'Noon to nine, seven days', 'Kitchen hours are 12:00 to 21:00 daily, CNE run included. An evening kickoff at BMO Field will not let out before we close, so plan us for before the gates, or after an afternoon fixture.', 'What actually survives an event day', 'Event food has to be eaten fast, carried, or shared standing up. These three do that better than the plates do. If you already know your gate time, put the order in ahead so the grill work is finished before you walk in.', 'Sandwiches::Chicken Shawarma', 'The $11.99 sandwich is the quick one. Order it, eat it walking down Jefferson and Liberty St, and you\'ll be through the Atlantic Ave entrance and onto the grounds before you finish it.', 'Sides::Add Popcorn Chicken', 'Six dollars. It settles the one person in the group who won\'t eat kebab, and it\'s the difference between a fed group at the gate and someone hungry two hours into a stadium seat.', 'Dessert::Baklava', 'Get it to go. It\'s the one thing here that travels properly in a bag — worth having on you three hours into a show at the Coliseum on Manitoba Drive.', 'I\'ve got a ticket to the Ex. Is it worth walking out and back?', 'If you\'re near the Atlantic Ave entrance to Exhibition GO or the Manitoba Drive gate, yes — six to ten minutes each way, and you eat off a charcoal grill instead of standing in a queue. Ask your own gate about same-day re-entry before you go; that\'s CNE policy and not ours to promise. The Ex runs from late August through Labour Day and we\'re open 12 to 9 on every one of those days.', 'We\'re at a 7:30 kickoff at BMO Field. Can we come after?', 'No — and better you hear it now than at 9:15 with the match still on. We close at 9pm every day, so an evening kickoff is out. The workable version is the other way round: eat around six, walk down for a 7:30 start, and you\'re in your seat with dinner already done. Afternoon fixtures and matinees at the Coliseum work fine on either side.', 'Can I have the order waiting when I get there?', 'Yes, and on an event day you should. Order through Square or the Google order page for pickup, or phone +1 416-516-2087. Everything is charcoal-grilled to order, so ordering ahead shifts the wait off your schedule. Pickup only — we don\'t run delivery through any of the apps.', 'Time it for an hour before your gate', '133 Jefferson Ave, up the west side of Lamport Stadium, one block north of the rail corridor from Exhibition Place. Noon to nine, seven days, fully halal, everything off the charcoal. Phone +1 416-516-2087 or order online for pickup — then walk down through Liberty Village and get to your gate with dinner already handled.', 'kebab-in-fort-york-toronto,kebab-in-parkdale-toronto')
