-- Fort York
INSERT INTO `neighbourhoods` (`slug`, `name`, `batch`, `sort_order`, `is_active`, `page_title`, `meta_desc`, `meta_keywords`, `og_image`, `og_image_alt`, `hero_eyebrow`, `hero_title`, `hero_text`, `hero_image`, `hero_image_alt`, `intro_title`, `intro_text`, `travel_title`, `travel_text`, `fact1_icon`, `fact1_label`, `fact1_text`, `fact2_icon`, `fact2_label`, `fact2_text`, `fact3_icon`, `fact3_label`, `fact3_text`, `fact4_icon`, `fact4_label`, `fact4_text`, `picks_title`, `picks_text`, `pick1_dish`, `pick1_note`, `pick2_dish`, `pick2_note`, `pick3_dish`, `pick3_note`, `faq1_q`, `faq1_a`, `faq2_q`, `faq2_a`, `faq3_q`, `faq3_a`, `closing_title`, `closing_text`, `neighbours`) VALUES
  ('kebab-in-fort-york-toronto', 'Fort York', 3, 5, 0, 'Kebab Near Fort York & Bathurst Quay, Toronto | Unika Kebab', 'Halal charcoal kebab about 2 km from Fort York — north over the Strachan Ave overpass to 133 Jefferson Ave, Liberty Village. Open 12-9 daily, pickup only.', 'kebab fort york, halal food bathurst quay, kebab near the bentway, turkish food fort york toronto', 'uploads/site/about_20260728_125447_4dd2b2.png', 'Kofte shaped by hand at Unika Kebab near Fort York', 'Across the corridor from Fort York', 'From Fort York, over the Strachan bridge to charcoal', 'Unika Kebab is at 133 Jefferson Ave in Liberty Village — not in your building\'s podium. Roughly 2 km from the Fort York Visitor Centre: about 25 minutes on foot over the Strachan Ave overpass. Halal, charcoal, open 12 to 9 daily.', 'uploads/site/about_20260728_125447_4dd2b2.png', 'Hand-shaped kofte at Unika Kebab, a short ride from Fort York', 'The ground floors around Fort York Blvd do not do dinner', 'Strachan Avenue is the reason this works. Until 2014 the rail corridor crossed it at grade; the Georgetown South project dropped the tracks into an eight-metre cut and lifted the road over them. So from Fort York you can walk north, over the corridor, and come out on King St W without waiting on a freight train. That is the route to us.

Our address is 133 Jefferson Ave, beside Allan A. Lamport Stadium in Liberty Village — the other side of those tracks, a different neighbourhood, and roughly 2 km from the fort\'s earth walls. We are not around the corner from you and we are not going to write it that way. What we are is one family-run halal charcoal grill, no second branch, with everything going over live coals when the order comes in.

Anyone living between Bathurst Street and Strachan knows why people make the trip. Thousands of units along Fort York Blvd, Fleet St and Dan Leckie Way, and a ground floor that fills with a pharmacy, a bank and a few cafés. Walk the loop past June Callwood Park at 636 Fleet St, through the Bentway, back up across Garrison Common, and you\'ll pass more heritage than hot food. Fort York keeps Canada\'s largest collection of original War of 1812 buildings. It does not keep a kebab shop.', 'North over the Strachan bridge, then west on King', 'From the Visitor Centre at 250 Fort York Blvd, go west to Fleet St, west again to Strachan Ave, then north. Strachan lifts you over the rail corridor and sets you down at King St W. Turn west: Shaw, Joe Shuster Way, Atlantic Ave, Fraser Ave, then Lamport Stadium on the south side. Jefferson Ave is the next street. Roughly 2 km all in — 25 to 30 minutes walking, eight to ten on a bike. Longer than the map suggests, because the corridor forces you out to Strachan first.

Not walking: the 509 Harbourfront leaves Fleet St at Fort York Blvd and runs west to Exhibition Loop at Manitoba Dr, about ten minutes on foot from us. Or take a westbound 504 King from King St W at Strachan Ave to the King St W at Jefferson Ave stop, right out front. Fleet St service has been rerouted for construction before, so check ttc.ca. Times are approximate.', 'fa-solid fa-person-walking', 'About 25 minutes on foot', 'Fort York Blvd to Fleet St, north on Strachan Ave over the rail cut, then west on King past Atlantic, Fraser and Lamport Stadium. Jefferson Ave is the next street. Roughly 2 km.', 'fa-solid fa-train', 'Strachan Ave crosses over the tracks', 'There used to be a level crossing here. The Georgetown South project sank the corridor about eight metres and raised Strachan over it, finished in 2014. That overpass is why the walk works.', 'fa-solid fa-train-subway', '509 from Fleet St at Fort York Blvd', 'The 509 Harbourfront runs west along Fleet St to Exhibition Loop at Manitoba Dr. From the loop it is about ten minutes on foot, up through Exhibition GO, to Jefferson Ave.', 'fa-solid fa-landmark', 'The Bentway ends where you turn', 'The Bentway occupies 1.75 km under the Gardiner from Strachan Ave to Bathurst St, with a 220-metre skate trail in winter. Come up at the Strachan end and you are already on the route.', 'The podium can\'t sell you any of this', 'None of this is coming out of a podium unit. If you\'re carrying dinner back over the bridge for more than one person, order at the plate end of the board — plates are built for a table, and sandwiches are really a lunch decision.', 'Plates (Platter)::Adana Kebab', 'The $24.99 plate, not the sandwich. Spicy, with rice and salad, and enough of it that the 2 km back over the Strachan overpass counts as working it off.', 'Plates (Platter)::Chicken Shawarma', 'The mild plate, $19.99. Order it alongside the Adana when the household splits on heat — one trip across the corridor, two people fed properly.', 'Dessert::Baklava', 'Add it while you\'re ordering, not after. We shut at nine and you\'re 25 minutes from Fort York Blvd — coming back for dessert is not a plan.', 'How long is the walk from Fort York, honestly?', 'About 25 to 30 minutes, and roughly 2 km. The straight-line distance is shorter, but the rail corridor means you have to go out to Strachan Ave and up over the overpass before you can head west on King St W. From the Strachan end of the neighbourhood, knock five minutes off. On a bike it\'s eight to ten, with the overpass as the only real climb. Estimates, not schedules.', 'Can I get there without walking over the bridge?', 'Yes. The 509 Harbourfront picks up at Fleet St at Fort York Blvd and runs west to Exhibition Loop at Manitoba Dr — about ten minutes on foot from there. From further east, around Eireann Quay and Bathurst Quay Common, it\'s the same streetcar and roughly 2.5 km. One caution: Fleet St service has been rerouted for construction more than once, so check ttc.ca before you build a plan on it.', 'We\'re at the Bentway in the evening — how late can we order?', 'Nine is the wall. We\'re open 12 to 9, seven days, and the grill needs a few minutes before that. From the skate trail under the Gardiner you\'re 25 minutes on foot or a streetcar ride away, so leave by eight if you want to sit down and eat it here. Put the order in first — Square, Google, or 416-516-2087 — and it\'s ready when you arrive.', 'Two kilometres and one overpass away', 'You know the stretch — Fort York Blvd, Fleet St, the Gardiner overhead, a ground floor that gives up by dinner. Go north over Strachan and there\'s a charcoal grill at 133 Jefferson Ave, beside Lamport Stadium. Halal, family run, open 12 to 9 every day of the week. Pickup only, and we\'re not on the delivery apps: order on Square or Google, or call 416-516-2087.', 'kebab-in-exhibition-place-toronto,kebab-in-king-west-toronto')
